.TH "REPROCTL\-LOGS" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
reproctl\-logs \- show or stream service logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]reproctl logs\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]] [\f[I]service\f[R]...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show or stream logs from running services.
Without \f[B]\-f\f[R] or explicit service names, displays the last 50
lines across all resources.
.PP
When service names are given, output is filtered to only those services.
When \f[B]\-f\f[R] / \f[B]\-\-follow\f[R] is specified, new log lines
are streamed in real time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-f\f[R], \f[B]\-\-follow\f[R]
Stream logs in real time instead of displaying a snapshot.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-level\f[R] \f[I]warn\f[R] | \f[I]error\f[R]
Filter log output to the specified severity level or above.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-source\f[R] \f[I]all\f[R] | \f[I]build\f[R] | \f[I]runtime\f[R]
Select the log source.
\f[B]all\f[R] (default) shows both build and runtime logs.
\f[B]build\f[R] shows only image build output.
\f[B]runtime\f[R] shows only container runtime output.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-grep\f[R] \f[I]pattern\f[R]
Filter log lines to those matching \f[I]pattern\f[R] (a regular
expression).
.TP
\f[B]\-C\f[R], \f[B]\-\-context\f[R] \f[I]duration\f[R]
Show \f[I]duration\f[R] of context around matching lines (implies
\f[B]\-\-grep\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]\-B\f[R] \f[I]duration\f[R]
Show \f[I]duration\f[R] of context before matching lines.
.TP
\f[B]\-A\f[R] \f[I]duration\f[R]
Show \f[I]duration\f[R] of context after matching lines.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-since\f[R] \f[I]duration\f[R] | \f[I]timestamp\f[R]
Only show logs newer than \f[I]duration\f[R] (e.g., \f[B]5m\f[R],
\f[B]1h\f[R]) or an absolute \f[I]timestamp\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]
Output logs in JSON format (one object per line).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-no\-prefix\f[R]
Omit the service\-name prefix from each log line.
.TP
\f[B]\-n\f[R], \f[B]\-\-tail\f[R] \f[I]lines\f[R]
Number of recent lines to display (default: \f[B]50\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]\-\-pick\f[R], \f[B]\-p\f[R]
Interactively select a service to view logs for.
Uses \f[B]fzf\f[R] if installed, otherwise a numbered prompt.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reproctl logs
Show the last 50 lines from all services.
.TP
reproctl logs \-f api\-server
Stream api\-server logs in real time.
.TP
reproctl logs \-\-json \-\-since 5m api\-server
Show structured JSON logs from the last 5 minutes.
.TP
reproctl logs \-\-level error
Show only error\-level logs across all services.
.TP
reproctl logs \-\-grep \(dqconnection refused\(dq \-C 10s
Search for a pattern with 10 seconds of surrounding context.
